From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 02:42:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan/runtime: refuse an imported pipeline binary key of the
 wrong size

vk_create_pipeline_binary copied key_size bytes of the key an application
passes through VkPipelineBinaryKeysAndDataKHR into the binary's own key,
which holds one blake3_hash, and only an assert guarded the copy. A release
build compiles the assert out, so a keySize above 32 wrote the excess over the
binary's other fields and past its allocation. The application chooses
keySize: the registry marks it noautovalidity, so no generated check bounds it,
and a Venus guest encodes it as a plain field beside a key array that always
holds VK_MAX_PIPELINE_BINARY_KEY_SIZE_KHR bytes.

Every key the runtime hands out is one blake3_hash, so a key of any other size
names no binary this runtime made. Refuse it before anything is allocated or
copied, with VK_ERROR_VALIDATION_FAILED. The command defines that result, and
it is the one a command gives when the implementation detects invalid usage;
an out-of-memory result would tell the caller that retrying may help, and
VK_ERROR_UNKNOWN would not tell an application fault from an implementation
failure. The binary is refused like any other the call cannot create: its
handle is null, the call returns the first failure, and the rest of the call
proceeds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c
index 367b9691c7a1e6e7e0b3f95b810d40117a6236d1..44474f4e89c3fe39d767d01f40c0161914a565c7 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c
@@ -4115,14 +4115,30 @@ vk_create_pipeline_binary(struct vk_device *device,
                           const VkAllocationCallbacks *alloc,
                           VkPipelineBinaryKHR *out_binary_h)
 {
+   /* Every key this runtime hands out is a blake3_hash, so a key of any other
+    * size names no binary it made.  An application chooses the size of the
+    * key it imports: the generated validation leaves keySize unchecked (the
+    * registry marks it noautovalidity), and a Venus guest encodes it as a
+    * plain field beside a key array that always holds
+    * VK_MAX_PIPELINE_BINARY_KEY_SIZE_KHR bytes.  Refuse it before anything is
+    * allocated or copied.  VK_ERROR_VALIDATION_FAILED is the result a command
+    * gives when the implementation detects invalid usage; it is one of the
+    * results this command defines, and unlike the out-of-memory results it
+    * does not tell the caller that retrying may help.
+    */
+   if (key_size != sizeof(blake3_hash)) {
+      return vk_errorf(device, VK_ERROR_VALIDATION_FAILED,
+                       "a pipeline binary key is %zu bytes, not %zu",
+                       key_size, sizeof(blake3_hash));
+   }
+
    struct vk_pipeline_binary *binary =
       vk_object_alloc(device, alloc, sizeof(*binary) + data_size,
                       VK_OBJECT_TYPE_PIPELINE_BINARY_KHR);
    if (binary == NULL)
       return vk_error(device, VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY);
 
-   assert(key_size == sizeof(binary->key));
-   memcpy(binary->key, key, key_size);
+   memcpy(binary->key, key, sizeof(binary->key));
 
    binary->size = data_size;
    memcpy(binary->data, data, data_size);
